autoregressive nature of language models and the generative efficacy of flow matching, FELLE effectively predicts continuous-valued tokens (mel-spectrograms). For each continuous-valued token, FELLE modifies the general prior distribution in flow matching by incorporating information from the previous step, improving coherence and stability. Furthermore, to enhance synthesis quality, FELLE introduces a coarse-to-fine flow-matching mechanism, generating continuous-valued tokens hierarchically, conditioned on the language model's output. Experimental results demonstrate the potential of incorporating flow-matching techniques in autoregressive mel-spectrogram modeling, leading to significant improvements in TTS generation quality, as shown in this https URL.\n \n\n \n \n \n Comments:\n Accepted by ACM Multimedia 2025\n \n\n Subjects:\n \n Computation and Language (cs.CL); Sound (cs.SD); Audio and Speech Processing (eess.AS)\n \n\n Cite as:\n arXiv:2502.11128 [cs.CL]\n \n\n \n  \n (or \n arXiv:2502.11128v2 [cs.CL] for this version)\n \n \n\n \n  \n https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2502.11128\n \n \n Focus to learn more\n \n \n \n arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\n\n \n\n \n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n Submission history\n From: Hui Wang [view email] \n [v1]\n Sun, 16 Feb 2025 13:54:32 UTC (341 KB)\n\n [v2]\n Wed, 3 Sep 2025 01:59:58 UTC (300 KB)\n\n \n\n \n \n \n Full-text links:\n Access Paper:\n\n \n \nView a PDF of the paper titled FELLE: Autoregressive Speech Synthesis with Token-Wise Coarse-to-Fine Flow Matching, by Hui Wang and 11 other authors\nView PDF\nHTML (experimental)\nTeX Source\n \n\n \n \n view license\n \n\n \n\n \n Current browse context:\n\n cs.CL\n\n \n\n < prev\n \n   |   \n next >\n \n\n \n\n new\n | \n recent\n | 2025-02\n \n\n Change to browse by:\n \n cs\n cs.SD\n eess\n eess.AS\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n References & Citations\n\n \n NASA ADS\nGoogle Scholar\n\n Semantic Scholar\n\n \n \n\n \n\n export BibTeX citation\n Loading...\n\n \n \n BibTeX formatted citation